Mac Mini Ubuntu Installation

Run these commands in your Ubuntu terminal to prepare the headless environment.

    Update your server and install the essential Linux dependencies (ffmpeg, xvfb, sqlite3, python3-venv).

    Create the project directory, build the virtual environment (python3 -m venv venv), and activate it.

    Install the Python packages via pip install -r requirements.txt.

    Create the voices/ directory and use wget to download the Piper TTS .onnx and .json voice models.

    Download the Cloudflared daemon directly from the official Cloudflare GitHub releases (cloudflared-linux-amd64.deb) and install it via dpkg.

    Authenticate Cloudflared (cloudflared tunnel login) and route your public domain to the local port (localhost:8000).

Automation & Security Setup

Ensure the server can recover from power outages and block malicious traffic.

    Configure UFW to explicitly allow OpenSSH (sudo ufw allow OpenSSH), then enable the firewall to block all other inbound ports.

    Create /etc/systemd/system/micro-diplomacy.service referencing your virtual environment's uvicorn binary to start the application automatically on boot.

    Make your backup script executable (chmod +x backup_db.sh) and add it to crontab -e to trigger at 2:00 AM nightly.
